+// RG_NATIVE_CPU's inline checkpoint (Rogue Galaxy: added). The native code's
+// back edges and calls subtract their charge from g_eeNativeBudget and call
+// out only when it runs out or g_eeCheckpointPending is set: the budget is
+// the cycles until the next thing that can come due (a deadline, the slice's
+// end, the timers' batch), so it runs out on the very checkpoint the
+// call-per-checkpoint scheme would have stopped at. EeScheduler folds what
+// was spent into its cycle clock before it reads it (settleNativeBudget) and
+// hands out a new budget before guest code runs again (grantNativeBudget).
+// The budget is the EE thread's; the pending flag is the scheduler's own,
+// set from any thread.
+
+#include <atomic>
+#include <cstdint>
+
+inline int64_t g_eeNativeBudget = 0;
+inline std::atomic<bool> g_eeCheckpointPending{false};
